	)
	(text "Low-impedance ceramic capacitors (X7R) are used as bulk decoupling capacitors close to \nthe MOSFETs to rapidly supply and absorb current transients caused by high-frequency switching.\n\nTheir low ESR and ESL help reduce voltage fluctuations and power dissipation, thereby limiting heating.\n\nHowever, their effective energy storage capacity is reduced, particularly due to DC bias. This trade-off \nis compensated by placing multiple capacitors in parallel to increase the total capacitance while \nmaintaining low impedance."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 24.13 173.99 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "63d1d9f6-e45d-44ec-8985-6d9ca96e9ca8")
	)
	(text "Ti example : 10k\nP = 3.3*3.3/10000 = 1.09mW\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 55.88 72.39 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "8cd1eb8a-bbea-4073-9725-2d5fa230f435")
	)
	(text "DC-Link Bulk Capacitor 36 x 4.7uF = 169.2 uF\n40% perte at 24V -> 117.72 uF"
